"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 30 at 7:37PM MDT until September 1 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of Colorado, including the following areas,\nCentral Colorado River Basin, Central Gunnison and Uncompahgre\nRiver Basin, Central Yampa River Basin, Debeque to Silt Corridor,\nFlat Tops, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, Gore and Elk\nMountains/Central Mountain Valleys, Grand Valley, Grand and\nBattlement Mesas, Northwest San Juan Mountains, Paradox\nValley/Lower Dolores River, Roan and Tavaputs Plateaus, Southwest\nSan Juan Mountains, Uncompahgre Plateau and Dallas Divide, Upper\nGunnison River Valley and West Elk and Sawatch Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains, Southeast\nUtah and Tavaputs Plateau.\n\n* WHEN...Through Monday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nRecent burn scars will also be especially susceptible and these\ninclude the Lee and Elk RX, Gold Mountain and Elk, Ferris, and\nBabylon burn scars to name a few.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Monsoonal moisture will remain across the area through Monday\nevening and will support thunderstorms and showers with heavy\nrainfall across the watch area. Several rounds of heavier rain\nare expected increasing the chance for flash flooding especially\nin our more susceptible areas.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-01T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Central Yampa River Basin; Roan and Tavaputs Plateaus; Grand Valley; Debeque to Silt Corridor; Central Colorado River Basin; Grand and Battlement Mesas; Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys; Central Gunnison and Uncompahgre River Basin; West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Flat Tops; Upper Gunnison River Valley; Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Southeast Utah; Tavaputs Plateau; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f7ff695e018105cca90d3b4c59e6816f865c6d8a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f7ff695e018105cca90d3b4c59e6816f865c6d8a.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-31T11:34:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 311134 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 534 AM MDT Mon Aug 31 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered to widespread precipitation chances return Monday, with higher coverage of precipitation across southeast UT and southwest CO than previous days. - Flash Flooding will continue to be possible as organized and training thunderstorms can produce he","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-31T07:09:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Showers and thunderstorms are on tap again today with heavy rain, gusty outflow winds, and lightning being the main concerns. Flash flooding will be possible under and near the strongest storms and showers. Moisture becomes limited Tuesday onwards with a noticeable downturn in convection expected. Fire weather concerns remain low. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOW","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"pgs01","station_name":"Pagosa Springs","distance_km":2.6,"soil_temp_5cm_f":60.87,"soil_temp_15cm_f":61.95,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":212.5,"wind_speed_mph":0.68,"air_temp_f":57.43,"relative_humidity":0.857,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.